 lyrics that often dealt with issues of feminism and the LGBT community. They mix punk's directness and politics with playful samples, eclectic pop, and lo-fi electronics. The group also adds multimedia and performance art elements to their live shows, which often features support from like-minded acts such as The Need. Le Tigre began touring together again in 2023.\r\n\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:40310","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":58331,"name":"Kathleen Hanna"},{"active":true,"id":526049,"name":"Johanna Fateman"},{"active":true,"id":656056,"name":"JD Samson"},{"active":false,"id":1057466,"name":"Sadie Benning"}],"namevariations":["Le Tigra","LeTigre"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/40310-Le-Tigre","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.letigre.world/","https://www.facebook.com/LeTigreWorld","https://www.instagram.com/letigreworld/","https://myspace.com/letigre","https://www.tiktok.com/@letigreworld","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Le_Tigre","https://twitter.com/letigreworld","https://www.youtube.com/channel/UChTahf3yGz238X-Sub4ZuGg"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/56550/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"56550","image":"https://i.discogs.com/_lf_2caEMpeMSjJqfQ1hI742IhdnDJx1Qs8zomOzIzI/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:480/w:480/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTU2NTUw/LTE3NTk3MDE4Njgt/OTcyMS5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/n6I03FdUX9bWGdgQSRalS_CLl0rBSTDXhOff5fXhKwE/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTU2NTUw/LTE3NTk3MDE4Njgt/OTcyMS5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Collaborative project with [url=https://www.discogs.com/artist/481809-Dennis-McFarlane]Dego[/url] as the central figure. On/off members are [url=https://www.discogs.com/artist/3515-Kaidi-Tatham]Kaidi Tatham[/url], [url=https://www.discogs.com/artist/299106-Akwasi-Mensah]Akwasi Mensah[/url] and [url=https://www.discogs.com/artist/43597-Matt-Lord]Matt Lord[/url], who also perform